{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510750-vtm-with-vtr-antagonists","id":1510750,"title":"VtM with VtR antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T18:49:27-07:00","id":1510750,"title":"VtM with VtR antagonists","content":"From what I've seen, there are a lot of people who aren't exactly Requiem fans, I'm not going to judge, however I came across one of their supplements called antagonists of the dark world, and I have to say, there are some ideas in there that I even I find it interesting and could yield some good chronicles. How would you use it or if you would use it? For those who don't know here are some examples that I found interesting.<br /> <br /> Aswang: A creature originating from the east, but that can be found practically all over the world, just like vampires they need blood to survive, but they need to feed more frequently (Several times a week) and unlike kindred they don't have a numbing bite and doesn't even bother to kill the victim which causes problems. All Aswang are women and their condition is passed from mother to daughter, they marry and have children with normal men and if they have a male child he is also born normally. The advantage they have over a vampire is that they are not affected by the sun or need to sleep and can pass for ordinary women during the day, but at night they transform and have a monstrous appearance that stands out.<br /> <br /> Toxic Mold: Basically a kind of supernatural fungus that feeds on dead flesh and very quickly being deadly to vampires because it can consume them in moments, it also releases toxic gases capable of killing if inhaled and a corrosive substance that corrodes and necroses the skin quickly. After reaching a certain size, it starts to have its own intelligence, even if primitive, it tries to consume and spread. The origin of the mold is unknown, as I recall.<br /> <br /> Rogue(I don't know the correct name in English): A creature that looks like a sick human and feeds on the organs of supernatural beings, usually starts with ghouls and then climbs from there and the worst part is that this creature learns from what it eats so if it consumed a kindred's heart, he wouldn't know everything, but he might discover some secrets. This creature can perfectly pass for a human, has no sense of empathy, and is immune to supernatural powers, but it is fragile to earthly weapons and can die from a well-placed gunshot. Its origin, objectives or number are left open.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T01:51:08-07:00","id":1510761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510750-vtm-with-vtr-antagonists#post1510750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aswang: A creature originating from the east, but that can be found practically all over the world, just like vampires they need blood to survive, but they need to feed more frequently (Several times a week) and unlike kindred they don't have a numbing bite and doesn't even bother to kill the victim which causes problems. All Aswang are women and their condition is passed from mother to daughter, they marry and have children with normal men and if they have a male child he is also born normally. The advantage they have over a vampire is that they are not affected by the sun or need to sleep and can pass for ordinary women during the day, but at night they transform and have a monstrous appearance that stands out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside we kind of already have weird alternative takes on the vampire from Asia, by way of Kindred of the East, I'm kind of wary of using a concept that's so extremely gendered. Like, &quot;all-woman monster race that seduces men to prey on them&quot; is...questionable in this day and age. Then again, I suppose that folklore in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Toxic Mold: Basically a kind of supernatural fungus that feeds on dead flesh and very quickly being deadly to vampires because it can consume them in moments, it also releases toxic gases capable of killing if inhaled and a corrosive substance that corrodes and necroses the skin quickly. After reaching a certain size, it starts to have its own intelligence, even if primitive, it tries to consume and spread. The origin of the mold is unknown, as I recall. </div> </div> </div>Liking this one. I think Vampire: The Masquerade doesn't make disease nearly as much of a problem as it probably should. It's a game about creatures that open the veins of many different people, on a constant basis, to quaff their fluids. They should be vectors, carriers, and even incubators for all manner of diseases, mundane and supernatural. But it's a conflict point that only sometimes comes up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fungus that eats flesh rooting itself in a dead creature&quot; sounds like a pretty appropriate extension of this theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rogue(I don't know the correct name in English): A creature that looks like a sick human and feeds on the organs of supernatural beings, usually starts with ghouls and then climbs from there and the worst part is that this creature learns from what it eats so if it consumed a kindred's heart, he wouldn't know everything, but he might discover some secrets. This creature can perfectly pass for a human, has no sense of empathy, and is immune to supernatural powers, but it is fragile to earthly weapons and can die from a well-placed gunshot. Its origin, objectives or number are left open.\u200b </div> </div> </div>A creature that is immune to supernatural powers but dies to a stiff breeze may not work super well, if its eventual main prey are vampires. All vampires can buff their Attributes, so even non-combat focused vampires are a physical threat to anything attacking them.<br /> <br /> Not to say it can't work. It would be interesting for such a creature to have to go around ambushing vampires and ghouls, because they know they can't take them in a straight up fight. Relying on taking them by surprise with how the main tools of many Clans (who specialize in mental or social powers) simply don't work. Plus, attacking during the day is a great way to catch a vampire while they're at their weakest and have limited options to flee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T10:11:53-07:00","id":1510804,"title":"","content":"One of the big things with NWoD which I personally see as a advantage over the CWoD is that it has a focus on mystery. As in there are tons and tons of stuff out there that we can't fit into a clearly defined niche in one cosmology or another.<br /> <br /> Personally I see absolutely no problem with bringing in stuff from VtR to a VtM game per principle. But then again I like crossover and love custom material for games, so I'm partial in that regard.<br /> <br /> As for using these specific threats some initial ideas are:<br /> <br /> <b>Aswang</b> - Definietly some kind of turf war as it seems to me that Cainites and Aswang have to many conflicting points, from the Masquerade to access to the human herd and so on that a conflict is invenitible if both sides are present in a decent number, especially if there is a decent number of Aswang. It seems to me that those creatures would draw hunters like moths to the flame and might also get themselves confused with the Nosferatu in some scenarios and thus become a matter for that Clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Mold</b> - I'm not sure how to run with this one. It might work if you're interested in some kind of Nurgle-esque antagonist who has developed a weapon to fight Cainites, or threathen Cainites with this weapon to make them mind their own business.<br /> <br /> <b>Rogue</b> - This could certainly work but given that Vampires base so much of their power on humans I would think that this antagonist might be more scary in a Mage game rather than a Vampire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T10:45:08-07:00","id":1510806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510750-vtm-with-vtr-antagonists?p=1510804#post1510804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big things with NWoD which I personally see as a advantage over the CWoD is that it has a focus on mystery. As in there are tons and tons of stuff out there that we can't fit into a clearly defined niche in one cosmology or another.<br /> <br /> Personally I see absolutely no problem with bringing in stuff from VtR to a VtM game per principle. But then again I like crossover and love custom material for games, so I'm partial in that regard.<br /> <br /> As for using these specific threats some initial ideas are:<br /> <br /> <b>Aswang</b> - Definietly some kind of turf war as it seems to me that Cainites and Aswang have to many conflicting points, from the Masquerade to access to the human herd and so on that a conflict is invenitible if both sides are present in a decent number, especially if there is a decent number of Aswang. It seems to me that those creatures would draw hunters like moths to the flame and might also get themselves confused with the Nosferatu in some scenarios and thus become a matter for that Clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Mold</b> - I'm not sure how to run with this one. It might work if you're interested in some kind of Nurgle-esque antagonist who has developed a weapon to fight Cainites, or threathen Cainites with this weapon to make them mind their own business.<br /> <br /> <b>Rogue</b> - This could certainly work but given that Vampires base so much of their power on humans I would think that this antagonist might be more scary in a Mage game rather than a Vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't put this in when I wrote it, because I didn't want to make the post too big, but Aswang don't have a community or anything like that, they either act alone, or in small groups like families, usually mother and daughter or sisters.<br /> <br /> The toxic mold, the tips that the supplement gives are that someone found it and decided to use it as a security system (I can think of a Nosferatu doing this) or even as a weapon, when small it looks like just a common fungus so someone could plant it in the lair, or even send it hidden in something kindred likes a lot. It also specifies that it can evolve and act as a parasite.\u200b<br /> <br /> Can you be more especfic about the rogue?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T12:50:59-07:00","id":1510811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510750-vtm-with-vtr-antagonists?p=1510806#post1510806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't put this in when I wrote it, because I didn't want to make the post too big, but Aswang don't have a community or anything like that, they either act alone, or in small groups like families, usually mother and daughter or sisters.<br /> <br /> The toxic mold, the tips that the supplement gives are that someone found it and decided to use it as a security system (I can think of a Nosferatu doing this) or even as a weapon, when small it looks like just a common fungus so someone could plant it in the lair, or even send it hidden in something kindred likes a lot. It also specifies that it can evolve and act as a parasite.\u200b<br /> <br /> Can you be more especfic about the rogue?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regarding the Aswang, a small group like a mother with 2-3 daughters or the same number of sisters should be perfectly enough to challenge both Cainites and the Masquerade if it takes place in a small town. Not every game needs to take place in a major metropolis. There are stories that works best in a metropolis, yes, but there are also stories that works best in other enviroments.<br /> <br /> True that one could use the Toxic Mold in that way. No objections from me.<br /> <br /> What I mean with the Rogue is that Cainites to a large degree, at least in the Camarilla and High Clans, are using humans and human-produced tools to a significent degree. That means that most Cainites will be able to get 3-5 mooks with weapons to kill the Rogue, or just ask someone else to fix this scenario or a small boon. Or just pull out a shotgun or a sword and kill the Rogue. That means that the Cainites are probably among those creatures of a supernatural nature that can most easily face off the Rogue by their access to resources from the human community.<br /> <br /> My experience with Mages is that they are more relient on their magic than Cainites are on their disicplines. Hence the Mages are more likely to get a scare from something that their supernatural powers can't effect, than Cainites are, as the Mages to a larger degree can't quickly mobilize human mooks with guns or swords (depending on the time period) to take care of the Rogue.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's how I see it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}